{
	title: 'Attachments: images and long pastes reach the model',
	spec: `A prompt can carry attachments. A client sends each once with an \`attach\` command { sessionId, mediaType, data (base64), name? }; the host checks it (png, jpeg, gif or webp images, or text/plain; at most 5 MB decoded; refused otherwise with a reason), stores it as sessions/<id>/blobs/<blobId>.<ext> with a random blob id, and answers that client with an \`attached\` event naming the command and the blob. The prompt text holds a marker for it: [image <blobId>] or [paste <blobId>, N lines]. When a prompt is submitted, the host resolves the markers of that session's blobs: an image becomes an image block { type: 'image', blob, mediaType } in the user record, and a paste becomes its text. History holds blob references, never the bytes. Providers read the bytes when they build a request: Anthropic as a base64 image source, OpenAI-compatible as an image_url data URL; replay and amend keep image blocks. A marker naming no blob of the session stays text, and the host tells the client.
The terminal shows a prompt's image blocks inside its card, after a blank row below the text, as labels like [image 12 kB png] packed into rows (a quick way to open the images its markers name); each label is an OSC 8 link (with the link code, task e3) to its /blob address. The web shows the image itself, served by an authenticated GET /blob/<sessionId>/<blobId> (the login cookie; only blobs of that session, only by exact id; no path from the request reaches the file system).
Tests: an attached png reaches both providers' request bodies as an image; history has no base64; a forged marker or a blob of another session is not resolved; the web route refuses a missing cookie and a path with slashes or dots. On the web an inline image is a keyboard-accessible native link that opens its authenticated image URL in a separate tab for isolated browser zoom. Inline image gestures allow vertical transcript panning, not whole-app pinch zoom; no lightbox or custom zoom library is needed.`,
	status: 'done',
	notes: [
		'old-attachments.ts resolved [path.png] markers pointing anywhere on disk and let .txt markers read files under /tmp/hal. Hal must not: only blobs the host stored for that session resolve. old-blob.ts and old-web-upload.ts are reference for storage and upload limits.',
		'The Anthropic API limits images to about 5 MB each and some OpenAI-compatible endpoints reject images; a provider without image support should get a text note in place of the image, not a failed request.',
		'Protocol messages are ASON over the socket and the WebSocket; a 5 MB base64 string is one large message. Measure that the socket framing and ason.parse handle it before choosing a smaller cap or chunking.',
		"Measured: a 5 MB attachment is ~7 MB of base64; ason.stringify takes ~4 ms and ason.parse ~16 ms, the socket line limit is 256 MB and Bun's WebSocket default maxPayloadLength 16 MB, so one attach message holds it without chunking.",
		'Image markers stay in the prompt text (the model can tell which image the words mean); the image blocks follow the texts in the user record. A paste marker stays a marker in history (task 31): history holds neither pasted text nor image bytes; history.messages expands paste markers to their text (blobs.expand) for the provider. Records written before that hold the text itself and still replay.',
		"An edit (amend) resolves the prompt's texts again: an image stays while its marker does, and deleting the marker drops it (what task zc wants). Resolution dedupes by blob id.",
		"ImageBlock carries an optional `bytes` (decoded size) so clients can label it without reaching the blob; turn-start and prompt events carry `images` so a live transcript equals a snapshot's.",
		'Providers get bytes through ProviderRequest.image(blob) (base64, read per request by blobs.base64); a missing file or an OpenAI-compatible endpoint with `images: false` becomes a <meta> text note (provider.imageNote).',
		"A marker naming no blob of the session is answered with a `warning` event to the submitting client only. attach is in host's `once` set: a resend gets the same `attached` event, nothing stored twice. The attach `name` is accepted but not stored.",
		'Blob ids are 12 lowercase hex digits; blobs.find tries each known extension, so the id is never joined to anything taken from a request. Stored bytes are checked against the media type (magic numbers, or valid UTF-8 for text/plain).',
		'The terminal image label links via itemView.itemLines when the session is known; without one it stays plain text.',
		'Image items keep their own keys (#26.1); frame.layout draws them in the preceding prompt card and draws nothing for them alone; a link to one scrolls to that card.',
		'UI exception (user, 2026-10-03): the web keeps one card per image, showing the image itself; only the terminal groups image labels inside the prompt card.'
	],
	needs: ['yq', '1b']
}
